# This file is an example, and it is not listed in kustomization.yaml, so
# `kubectl apply -k k8s/` never creates it. That is the point of it.
#
# WHY THERE IS NO SECRET IN THIS STACK
#
# The roadmap called for `k8s/secret.yaml` holding "credentials (H2 / OpenRouter /
# gateway)". Checked against the code, none of those three exists as a cluster
# secret:
#
#   * H2 runs in-memory with the default `sa` user and no password. There is
#     nothing to protect, and a Secret holding an empty password protects it.
#   * OpenRouter is real, but it is a *CI* secret: .github/scripts/ai-review.py
#     posts pull-request diffs to it from GitHub Actions, reading
#     `secrets.OPENROUTER_API_KEY`. No deployed service ever calls it, so the key
#     belongs to GitHub Secrets and must not be copied into the cluster.
#   * The gateway has no authentication, no API keys and no TLS material.
#
# An applied-but-empty Secret would be decoration — it would look like security
# review had happened. This file exists instead: the mechanism is written down,
# ready for the day the engine points at a real database.
#
# WHEN THAT DAY COMES
#
#   1. Create the Secret out of band — never committed, never in this repository:
#
#        kubectl -n tik-tak-toe create secret generic engine-datasource \
#          --from-literal=SPRING_DATASOURCE_USERNAME=games \
#          --from-literal=SPRING_DATASOURCE_PASSWORD='...'
#
#      (Or apply the manifest below with real values from a secrets manager.
#      `stringData` is plain text on the way in; Kubernetes stores it base64 in
#      etcd, which is encoding, not encryption — etcd encryption at rest is a
#      cluster setting, not something a manifest can ask for.)
#
#   2. Add it to game-engine-service.yaml beside the existing `envFrom`:
#
#        envFrom:
#          - configMapRef:
#              name: eureka-client
#          - secretRef:
#              name: engine-datasource
#
#      Spring's relaxed binding maps those names onto spring.datasource.username
#      and .password, so — as everywhere else in this milestone — no
#      application.yml changes.
#
# ---8<--- the manifest itself, for reference ---8<---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: engine-datasource
type: Opaque
stringData:
  SPRING_DATASOURCE_USERNAME: replace-me
  SPRING_DATASOURCE_PASSWORD: replace-me
